\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}Standard number systems are $\mathbb N,\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$. Specialized notation and index ranges follow the cited source and the definitions below.


An extractor maps a specified class of weak random sources to output close to uniform under the chosen distance. A seedless extractor has no additional independent random seed. Output length and error are distinct parameters, governed by the allowed source assumptions.
\paragraph{Record scope and qualifications.}
The catalogue title is retained as metadata. Named certificates, contracts, bounds or frameworks in that title are not asserted as results of the original source extract.
The source family, entropy assumptions, and baseline parameters are absent. No extractor for arbitrary unconstrained distributions is asserted.

Source-record limitation: Output and error improvement for seedless extractors lacks the source family, min-entropy assumptions, and baseline parameters; without them there is no recoverable mathematical target.
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Improve the output length and error parameters of seedless extractors. \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2024/27}{[S2]}
\paragraph{Source status.}
The supplied catalogue labels this source record open; that metadata was checked against the supplied snapshot on 2026-10-11. The label is preserved for provenance and is not an independent verification of present open status or mathematical correctness. The catalogue literature assessment is dated 2026-08-22.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Improve the output and error of the stated seedless-extraction setting.

